# Providers' commands (decision 160): published to the host, run by another
# provider (Search) for the user, and passing the user's gesture to their owner.

scenario: a provider's list replaces its last; bad and repeated ids are dropped
publish-commands timer open,pause      -> commands=timer/open,timer/pause
publish-commands timer open,resume     -> commands=timer/open,timer/resume   # what applies now
publish-commands theme toggle,toggle,bad/id, -> commands=theme/toggle,timer/open,timer/resume
publish-commands timer none!           -> commands=theme/toggle             # nothing valid: none
stop-provider theme                    -> commands=none                     # its commands go with it

scenario: a command runs only right after the user acted on the caller
publish-commands timer open
run-command search timer open          -> ran=notnow                        # from a wake-up or a reply: refused
acted search
run-command search timer open          -> ran=ran
wait 3001
acted search
wait 3001
run-command search timer open          -> ran=notnow                        # too long after: windowOpenGrace

scenario: one user action runs one command
publish-commands timer open,pause
acted search
run-command search timer open          -> ran=ran
run-command search timer pause         -> ran=notnow                        # no chain from one click
wait 1
acted search
run-command search timer pause         -> ran=ran                           # the next click runs the next

scenario: running a command lets its owner open a window, as a click on its card would
publish-commands timer open
acted search
open-window timer full                 -> opened=notnow                     # Search's click isn't Pomodoro's
run-command search timer open          -> ran=ran
open-window timer full                 -> opened=opened windows=timer/full
open-window search results             -> opened=opened                     # the caller keeps its own

scenario: a provider doesn't run its own commands, or ones that aren't there
publish-commands timer open
acted timer
run-command timer timer open           -> ran=own
acted search
run-command search timer gone          -> ran=unknown
run-command search notes open          -> ran=unknown
run-command search timer open          -> ran=ran                           # a refused run doesn't spend the action
